ss passed the War Powers  Resolution which requires the President  to notify Congress within 48 hours of  sending troops into hostile territory  following the 9/11 attacks Congress  passed the authorization for use of  military force  giving the president broad authority in  specific cases the AUMF as it's known  has been used 41 times in 18 countries  Supreme Court has never ruled directly  on the president's war powers before  legal experts say that is by design to  keep justices out of the fight but hey  Bret it's the Supreme Court anything  could happen behind me okay respond live  outside the Supreme Court David thank  you
 

